Notebook[{
Cell["IsomorphicHypergraphQ", "ObjectName",ExpressionUUID->"85990c39-1161-1f45-baf4-9b29278e9369"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"IsomorphicHypergraphQ", "[", 
    RowBox[{"hg1", ",", " ", "hg2"}], "]"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"90737941-118a-e442-bcb3-b2561fafd68c"],
 " ",
 "gives True if hg1 and hg2 are isomorphic as labelled hypergraphs."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"e51e0c28-f545-0d43-8064-d170e3e3bcde"],

Cell["Details and Options", "NotesSection",ExpressionUUID->"1efad403-e7a0-9247-a86d-4a2122447b80"],

Cell["\<\
Some renaming of vertex identifiers must carry hg1 onto hg2: the edge \
multisets must match exactly, each edge matching up to its own symmetry type, \
with edge multiplicities preserved.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"72566caf-452f-2a43-8a27-beea54c0e1c0"],

Cell["\<\
The renaming must also carry the labels of hg1 onto those of hg2 by a \
one-to-one correspondence. Labels are therefore significant only up to \
renaming: what must agree is which elements share a label, not what the \
labels are called.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"96683852-f1e3-e844-a674-a8670cdd63b5"],

Cell["\<\
Vertex labels and edge labels are put in correspondence independently of one \
another.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"3cc81cb1-43e4-f34f-bf27-03c5ed4addcc"],

Cell["\<\
An element with no label can correspond only to an element with no label. \
Without this, every unlabelled hypergraph would be isomorphic to a labelled \
one whose labels were all alike.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"ce9d000c-7886-f04e-ae6e-5f9db3f68f8f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "With ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"\"\<Labeled\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "False"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"1a637ba0-7e54-a24c-998a-055c0e35bee3"],
 " the skeletons are compared instead, ignoring labels altogether. Labelled \
isomorphism always implies isomorphism of skeletons."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"5b3df320-b950-d14d-bab1-a3f13f0c5018"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Method", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "499e08c4-5f47-194b-8bc8-fc501a3038fc"],
 " option is as for CanonicalHypergraph. Both settings always agree here."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"dd7a520b-f738-e84c-b697-61c3463923bb"],

Cell["\<\
The search is exhaustive, and is comfortable up to roughly eight vertices.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"b8fef7a6-95d2-6b47-a015-7eed4815af3c"],

Cell["Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection",ExpressionUUID->"8f8480a1-2cc1-1f4c-9df2-bab767ff5723"],

Cell["The same directed path on different identifiers:", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"ac1dc5cf-873a-3942-b9eb-01fcba537677"],

Cell["\<\
{IsomorphicHypergraphQ[Hypergraph[{{1, 2}, {2, 3}}], Hypergraph[{{10, 20}, \
{20, 30}}]],
 IsomorphicHypergraphQ[Hypergraph[{{1, 2}, {2, 3}}], Hypergraph[{{1, 2}, {1, \
3}}]]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"4ab6395b-e3fc-4043-816f-530c9544af78"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"True", ",", "False"}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"e165a04f-\
9b33-7544-a43f-7d4394db913c"],

Cell["\<\
Symmetry types are respected: a directed path is not an unordered one, but an \
unordered path on three vertices is an unordered star:\
\>", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"828cbdf1-68ad-6a41-880e-f5dd898a1d1a"],

Cell["\<\
{IsomorphicHypergraphQ[Hypergraph[{{1, 2}, {2, 3}}],
                       Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}, \"Unordered\"], Edge[{2, 3}, \
\"Unordered\"]}]],
 IsomorphicHypergraphQ[Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}, \"Unordered\"], Edge[{2, 3}, \
\"Unordered\"]}],
                       Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}, \"Unordered\"], Edge[{1, 3}, \
\"Unordered\"]}]]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"48ca1ed5-37f8-a04f-a583-2ae46d440b63"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"False", ",", "True"}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"7ca6d2a0-\
ed0d-7e49-9fbc-363a7c1b1966"],

Cell["\<\
Labels count only up to a one-to-one renaming. Here a, b corresponds to x, y:\
\
\>", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"f4e8e118-e86e-5349-b690-425999b044df"],

Cell["\<\
h1 = Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}, \"Directed\", \"a\"], Edge[{2, 3}, \
\"Directed\", \"b\"]}];
h2 = Hypergraph[{Edge[{4, 5}, \"Directed\", \"x\"], Edge[{5, 6}, \
\"Directed\", \"y\"]}];
IsomorphicHypergraphQ[h1, h2]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"04c0c62f-fa31-cb4c-b74a-a89932aec3bf"],

Cell[BoxData["True"], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"0eab3dc3-2528-a041-a986-b97529458ec5"],

Cell["\<\
But h3 repeats a single label where h1 has two distinct ones, and no \
correspondence can do that:\
\>", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"04973a71-b070-e043-9b83-8109279d032f"],

Cell["\<\
h3 = Hypergraph[{Edge[{4, 5}, \"Directed\", \"x\"], Edge[{5, 6}, \
\"Directed\", \"x\"]}];
{IsomorphicHypergraphQ[h1, h3], IsomorphicHypergraphQ[h1, h3, \"Labeled\" -> \
False]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"1ac44e0a-c906-7a4f-b21c-f35b949700a4"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"False", ",", "True"}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"67832f9b-\
b855-cf47-97b9-923ac8f22a93"],

Cell["\<\
The same principle governs vertex labels. A, A, B against A, B, B is not an \
isomorphism, because A would have to correspond to both A and B:\
\>", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"19acf66d-2ee3-2b4f-9d98-9c5c7dfad438"],

Cell["\<\
{IsomorphicHypergraphQ[
   Hypergraph[{Vertex[1, \"A\"], Vertex[2, \"A\"], Vertex[3, \"B\"]}, {{1, \
2}, {2, 3}}],
   Hypergraph[{Vertex[1, \"A\"], Vertex[2, \"B\"], Vertex[3, \"B\"]}, {{1, \
2}, {2, 3}}]],
 IsomorphicHypergraphQ[
   Hypergraph[{Vertex[1, \"A\"], Vertex[2, \"B\"], Vertex[3, \"C\"]}, {{1, \
2}, {2, 3}}],
   Hypergraph[{Vertex[1, \"C\"], Vertex[2, \"B\"], Vertex[3, \"A\"]}, {{1, \
2}, {2, 3}}]]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"9eed5c64-0a61-c341-b1a9-50f3c9844d7b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"False", ",", "True"}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"25b4bc36-\
969c-9549-b7af-dfaa8eab783b"],

Cell["An unlabelled edge is not a labelled one:", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"4fc4a793-eca4-7f42-9d0f-f96377a5517e"],

Cell["\<\
{IsomorphicHypergraphQ[Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}, \"Directed\", \"f\"]}], \
Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}]}]],
 IsomorphicHypergraphQ[Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}, \"Directed\", \"f\"]}], \
Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}]}],
                       \"Labeled\" -> False]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"d7e1fcf5-a641-5842-9807-acc116a30db5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"False", ",", "True"}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"b3147d11-\
63ea-cf4f-aa9a-9f61a858473a"],

Cell["Source", "NotesSection",ExpressionUUID->"bd51a83d-2dd2-824e-9d72-69b87baf3be4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Defined in ",
 StyleBox["src/Hypergraph.wl",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Plain"],
 ", section ",
 "\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]",
 "Canonical form and isomorphism",
 "\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"e33b1c4d-203b-194a-af5e-815aef579b7b"],

Cell["See Also", "SeeAlsoSection",ExpressionUUID->"ebe98ea6-c39d-4448-bcdd-a00e6cb8aa48"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["FindHypergraphIsomorphism", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"cf795d50-dce2-304d-ae68-c590a731a0f6"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["CanonicalHypergraph", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"cfd011e2-d43d-2441-b386-f7e02a1afce9"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["HypergraphSkeleton", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"78b97c6d-a800-da4f-89ce-f8edeb5d3f6e"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Hypergraph", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "7bf0d87c-3791-be44-b1b9-98814d94bcc8"]
}], "SeeAlso",ExpressionUUID->"e22c7c34-5e0b-b641-a482-8feea087fab8"]
},
WindowSize->{800, 750},
